 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "They look familiar",
     "texto": [
      "Thousands of Spanish and English words are true cousins: **importante**, **posible**, **universidad**. A few dozen are traps, and they are very common words.\n\nSome are embarrassing: **embarazada** is «pregnant» and **constipado** is «having a cold».\n\nSome quietly change your meaning: **actualmente** is «currently», **eventualmente** is «possibly», **largo** is «long», **sensible** is «sensitive».\n\nSome are verbs you will use every day: **asistir a** (to attend), **realizar** (to carry out), **soportar** (to put up with), **pretender** (to intend), **discutir** (to argue), **recordar** (to remember, not «to record»), **contestar** (to answer).\n\nAnd some are nouns: **la librería**, **la carpeta**, **el éxito**, **la noticia** (a piece of news), **los parientes**, **la decepción** (disappointment), **el compromiso** (commitment)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "What each word really means",
     "texto": [
      "Learn each pair whole: what it **does** mean and what it does **not**.\n\n- **embarazada** = pregnant (not «embarrassed»: avergonzado)\n- **actualmente** = currently (not «actually»: en realidad)\n- **sensible** = sensitive (not «sensible»: sensato)\n- **librería** = bookshop (not «library»: biblioteca)\n- **éxito** = success (not «exit»: salida)\n- **asistir a** = to attend (not «to assist»: ayudar)\n- **realizar** = to carry out (not «to realise»: darse cuenta)\n- **soportar** = to put up with (not «to support»: apoyar)\n- **pretender** = to intend (not «to pretend»: fingir)\n- **largo** = long (not «large»: grande)\n- **discutir** = to argue (not «to discuss»: hablar de)\n- **parientes** = relatives (not «parents»: padres)\n\nWatch the prepositions: **asistir a** a meeting, **soportar** the noise (no preposition)."
     ],
